  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "India and Egypt form working group to explore trade deal contours",
      "link": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/piyush-goyal-in-egypt-for-india-egypt-joint-trade-committee-jtc-meet/article71706845.ece",
      "description": "During his ongoing visit to Egypt, Commerce Minister Piyush Goyal co-chaired, along with Egypt’s Minister of Investment and Foreign Trade Mohamed Farid Saleh, the 7th session of the India-Egypt Joint Trade Committee (JTC) in Egypt’s New Administrative Capital.",
      "source_name": "The Hindu National",
      "published": "2026-11-16T17:16:42"
    },
    {
      "title": "India, Egypt may ease startup entry under proposed trade pact: Piyush Goyal",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/economy/news/india-egypt-may-ease-startup-entry-under-proposed-trade-pact-piyush-goyal-126111601343_1.html",
      "description": "India and Egypt can discuss providing a facilitative environment for startups for entry into each other's territories, in areas such as government procurement, under the proposed trade pact between the two countries, Commerce and Industry Minister Piyush Goyal said on Monday.\nAddressing the Egypt-India Startup Forum, he said the two sides will need to have their officials work out how startups from both countries can be given opportunities to operate and collaborate with each other.\nHe added that India has provided opportunities for domestic startups, as many are engaged with consumers directly.\n\"... in every marketplace, we have tried to ease the entry of startups so that they can prove their concept and prove their product... We are looking at an agreement between Egypt and India for a preferential or a free trade going forward.\n\"We will discuss the entry of startups in each other's territories....and give them an opportunity to get into maybe government procurement or help them",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-16T11:53:46"
    },
    {
      "title": "Goyal urges India, Egypt fintechs to build cross-border payment systems",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/external-affairs-defence-security/news/goyal-urges-india-egypt-fintechs-to-build-cross-border-payment-systems-126111601183_1.html",
      "description": "Commerce and Industry Minister Piyush Goyal on Monday urged the fintechs of India and Egypt to co-create and co-build cross-border payment systems to increase collaborations between entrepreneurs of the two countries.\nHe said both countries can look at facilitating entry of startups in each other's territories and participate in areas like government procurement.\nAddressing Egypt-India Startup Forum here, he said India's UPI journey and Egypt's InstaPay share one vision.\n\"If our fintechs co-create, co-build cross-border payment systems riding on the technology created, coupled with local currencies trade in goods and services, that we have recently launched, can certainly help our trade to go up significantly and digital payments may get popular all across Egypt at almost no cost,\" Goyal said.\nHe also suggested that entrepreneurs of two sides explore co-creating and co-innovating, precision irrigation, desalination, and cold chains.\nHealth tech and pharma is an area where together",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-16T09:34:37"
    }
  ]
